  <info>
    <title type="text">Basic Calculator Help</title>
    <desc>Help for the multilingual Python calculator.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Basic Calculator</title>

  <p>
    Basic Calculator is an open-source graphical application
    developed using Python and Tkinter. It performs basic
    arithmetic operations and supports English, Hindi, and Marathi.
  </p>

  <section id="features">
    <title>Features</title>
    <list>
      <item><p>Addition using the plus (+) operator.</p></item>
      <item><p>Subtraction using the minus (-) operator.</p></item>
      <item><p>Multiplication using the asterisk (*) operator.</p></item>
      <item><p>Division using the slash (/) operator.</p></item>
      <item><p>Language selection between English, Hindi, and Marathi.</p></item>
      <item><p>Localized digits for Hindi and Marathi.</p></item>
      <item><p>Error handling for invalid expressions and division by zero.</p></item>
    </list>
  </section>

  <section id="usage">
    <title>How to Use</title>
    <steps>
      <item><p>Launch the calculator application.</p></item>
      <item><p>Select the desired language from the dropdown menu.</p></item>
      <item><p>Enter numbers using the calculator buttons.</p></item>
      <item><p>Select an arithmetic operator.</p></item>
      <item><p>Enter the next number and press the equals button.</p></item>
      <item><p>Use Clear to remove the complete expression.</p></item>
      <item><p>Use Delete Last to remove the last character.</p></item>
    </steps>
  </section>

  <section id="errors">
    <title>Error Handling</title>
    <p>
      The calculator displays an error message when an invalid
      mathematical expression is entered or division by zero
      is attempted.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="open-source">
    <title>Open-Source Development</title>
    <p>
      Git is used for source-code version control. The application
      includes translation resources, Mallard help documentation,
      and Debian package support.
    </p>
  </section>

</page>
